cornell

# What the program writes. An image is a result, not a source: every one of
# these is one command away from existing again, and none of them belong in
# the history.
*.ppm
*.pfm
*.exr

# What a person converts them to in order to look at them, because macOS
# will not open a PPM. Not writing these down is how `propose` ends up
# refusing on a dirty tree for a reason that has nothing to do with the work.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg

.DS_Store
compile_commands.json

# Worktrees live here: one per item, and each one is a full checkout that
# `git status` in the parent would otherwise report as a pile of untracked
# files. They are not the work; the pull request is.
.claude/worktrees/
